{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["Gad, a troop — the troop of Israel will troop after him when they go forth to the war of Joshua, as it is written: ״חלוצים תעברו לפני אחיכם״, and when Gad returns from the battle, the men of Gad return after the rear guard of Israel, for such is the way: when they go out to war they go out first, and on their return they are last, to guard the tribes from the enemy, lest the enemy pursue them."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "The lemma reflects the concise form גד גדוד; the full verse phrase is גד גדוד יגודנו."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:47.493104566Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}